Z||000006||FormulaJoe||11-09-2001||01:04 PM||||     Bszopi, when I first visited the site 87gtz34 suggested I was overwhelmed by all the info.  I printed the pin-out page for the 16149396 ECM (which says at the top of that page that it is a 1227727?),  but didnt really understand it.  After looking at the page that was suggested by leadfoot I understand the data from the other site  a little better now.  Terryk I would like a copy of that email too, if you dont mind, and anything else you can suggest to make this swap easier.<BR>     Something that I noticed and was wondering about is weather a 1227727 ECM could be used instead of a 16149396 ECM?  I saw where the 9396 ECM has more SRAM memory but is essentially the same ECM.  Reason I am asking is the (I think, I could be wrong) 1227727 ECMs are plentiful and are used  when retrofitting injection to small block Chevy engines by hotrodders so there is a wealth of information and aftermarket parts  for them.  Right now I do not have an ECM and wiring harness so could easily go either way.  Just wondering if there would be any benifit to do so?||||reg||6
Z||000007||bszopi||11-09-2001||01:10 PM||||The '396 is in fact the same as the '727 with the extra RAM. The extra RAM is used to control the electronic transmissions. That is the reason I need to use the '396. The swap I am doing is from a 94 3100 ECM which is a FLASH ECM, to the '396, which is able to be programmed. So no, I don't have a Fiero (94 Beretta actually), but it seems like you guys have done swaps utilizing this ECM before, so I figured I'd ask. I need to extra RAM to control my 4T60-E. So, the diagrams of the '727s that I already have do not include all the pin info for the E-trannies. Thanks to everyone who has helped out with this!! I really appreciate it, and I look forward to that email Terry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Brad||||reg||1
Z||000008||conductor||11-09-2001||03:17 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.furtunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fieroparts.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.furtunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/fieroparts.htm</A> <BR>Search somewhere on this site under conversions or electrical wiring.<BR>Good luck.||||reg||7
Z||000009||conductor||11-09-2001||03:22 PM||||Ok, I forgot the <A HREF="http://," TARGET=_blank>http://,</A>  and fieroparts must be fierowiring||||reg||6
Z||000010||terryk||11-09-2001||03:53 PM||||No problem. I just have to pull the manuals out of my attic.<P>The 9396 *is* just a 7727 with more ram. In fact we ran the Grand Prix Turbo code in the 9396 ECM when we were considering turbocharging the DOHC. A few tweaks and it ran fine.<P>Are you planning on running DOHC code to run the 3100 or just making an observation about the 3100 using the same ECM for a year?||||reg||1
Z||000011||bszopi||11-09-2001||05:41 PM||||Actually, I will be running the 3100SFI with modified 3.1MPFI code. I am making a pigtail harness for the '396 which will be able to plug into my existing harness w/o any cutting. That way, if I can't get the chip tuned right away, I will be able to unplug the '396 and plug the old ECM back in. Since we can't find any BIN info on the 3100, we are just going to work with the 3.1 code and hope we can get it to work. I will be loosing some things (cam position sensor) therefore it will operate as a multi-port system vice the sequential system, but in the long run, I think being able to tune the car for performance will be worth it. <P>I'll check out that other site tonight also....||||reg||1
Z||000012||terryk||11-09-2001||06:30 PM||||I have the 3100 SD and MAF bins. <P>Are you using HEI/MAP or DIS/MASS?||||reg||1
Z||000013||bszopi||11-09-2001||08:40 PM||||I am actually running DIS and MAP. Odd that you ask about HEI, since I don't think a 3100 ever came with HEI... Is the 3100 code set up similar to the 3.1 or 3.4 code? As in locations for VE, MAP, and all that other stuff (I'm not a master of the chip yet, but a freind is). That would be great if he could look at 3100 code and manipulate it to work for me. Thanks for all the help!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||terryk||11-09-2001||10:14 PM||||Ah, I see what you mean. Right, the "3100 SFI" only came in DIS/Mass form. The 3.1L came in both (SD/HEI in F bodies).<P>I used to run my X-11 MPFI on the 7730 and the HEI/SD code. I have the schematics for that somewhere too. I have too much stuff.....<P>I don't think the 3100 uses the same code as the DOHC. I know the DOHC code, but not the 3100 very well. I don't recall it being the same, but as always GM tends to do stuff the same way so he should be able to find it.||||reg||1
Z||000015||mrossum||11-10-2001||09:49 AM||||i could sure use some chip programming help. am using a 7727 brain in my stroked 2.5 w/5.0 tbi unit. HELP..........charley j||||reg||1
